---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/seo/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Our Private File Converters"
  description={`${siteConfig.name} is maintained by ${siteConfig.defaultAuthor.name}: privacy-first niche file converters that run in your browser—your file never leaves your device.`}
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <div class="container content-prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About' }]} />
    <h1>About {siteConfig.name}</h1>
    <div class="answer-box">
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} is a free collection of profession-specific file converters that run entirely in your browser.
        Maintained by {siteConfig.defaultAuthor.name}, it focuses on format pairs (YAML↔JSON, PSD→PNG, STL utilities,
        bank-statement PDF text extraction) where privacy and accuracy beat generic upload farms.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>Why we built this</h2>
    <p>
      Sensitive configs, unpublished design comps, and financial PDFs should not be uploaded to unknown servers just to
      change formats. Client-side conversion (JS/WASM) keeps file bytes on-device after the tool code loads. Page analytics,
      when configured, are separate from conversion — they measure visits, not your documents.
    </p>
    <h2>Who builds it</h2>
    <p>
      {siteConfig.defaultAuthor.fullName} ({siteConfig.defaultAuthor.name}) maintains the converters, documentation, and
      fixtures as an independent developer. There is no claim of affiliation with Adobe, Apple, banks, or CAD vendors.
      See <a href="/authors/">Authors</a> for profiles and contact.
    </p>
    <h2>What we ship</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Data: YAML↔JSON, CSV↔JSON, XML→JSON, TOML→JSON</li>
      <li>Images: HEIC→JPG, PSD→PNG, SVG→PNG, WebP/PNG/JPG</li>
      <li>Documents: Markdown→HTML (GFM), PDF bank statement text→CSV</li>
      <li>CAD: STL viewer, STL→OBJ, ASCII/binary STL, educational STL→G-code</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
    <p>
      Every tool page includes method notes, limits, worked examples, FAQs, and links to authoritative format specs. Guides
      expand comparison and how-to queries with topic-specific steps. See <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> for how
      we test converters and handle corrections.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact &amp; bugs</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> or visit
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>. Include the page URL and error text only — never attach confidential files.
    </p>
    <p class="meta-row">Last updated: <time datetime={siteConfig.lastUpdated}>{siteConfig.lastUpdated}</time></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
